sible, and apps can still read them over the REST API — but no new ones can be submitted, because the review form needs comments to be open on the product.','Product reviews are currently enabled.'=>'Product reviews are currently enabled.','Product reviews are currently disabled.'=>'Product reviews are currently disabled.','Product reviews are turned off in WooCommerce\'s own settings, so customers cannot leave one regardless of what is set here.'=>'Product reviews are turned off in WooCommerce\'s own settings, so customers cannot leave one regardless of what is set here.','WooCommerce Product Reviews'=>'WooCommerce Product Reviews','This is the reverse of the setting above. A comment type closed here stops being accepted even where comments are otherwise open, and everything else on the same posts keeps working — so a WooCommerce store can close product reviews while other comments on products stay open. Existing comments of that type are not deleted; on a product page WooCommerce\'s Reviews tab is hidden while the type is closed. A type ticked in both lists counts as closed.'=>'This is the reverse of the setting above. A comment type closed here stops being accepted even where comments are otherwise open, and everything else on the same posts keeps working — so a WooCommerce store can close product reviews while other comments on products stay open. Existing comments of that type are not deleted; on a product page WooCommerce\'s Reviews tab is hidden while the type is closed. A type ticked in both lists counts as closed.','No separately closeable comment types were found on this site.'=>'No separately closeable comment types were found on this site.','Comment types that can be closed'=>'Comment types that can be closed','Close Certain Comment Types'=>'Close Certain Comment Types','Closed Comment Types Settings'=>'Closed Comment Types Settings','Download a CSV backup first'=>'Download a CSV backup first','Preview what will be deleted'=>'Preview what will be deleted','Comment types you have allowed are left out of both: they cannot be deleted from here.'=>'Comment types you have allowed are left out of both: they cannot be deleted from here.','Comments on this site:'=>'Comments on this site:','Comments across this network:'=>'Comments across this network:','What is blocking reviews: "disable-comments" for this plugin\'s settings, "woocommerce" for WooCommerce\'s own review switch, or an empty string when reviews are enabled. Tells an agent which setting to point the user at.'=>'What is blocking reviews: "disable-comments" for this plugin\'s settings, "woocommerce" for WooCommerce\'s own review switch, or an empty string when reviews are enabled. Tells an agent which setting to point the user at.','True when WooCommerce is running on this site. The review fields below only mean anything while it is.'=>'True when WooCommerce is running on this site. The review fields below only mean anything while it is.','Comments close automatically on posts older than this many days. Zero means no age limit. A post kept open by an explicit exception rule stays open past this window.'=>'Comments close automatically on posts older than this many days. Zero means no age limit. A post kept open by an explicit exception rule stays open past this window.','True when customers cannot leave a WooCommerce product review. Reviews are usually just comments on the "product" post type, so this is mostly the answer for reviews specifically, which "disabled_post_types" does not give you in a form a store owner would recognise. It can also be true on its own: "review" appearing in "blocked_comment_types" closes reviews while comments on products stay open, and WooCommerce\'s own review setting being off closes them regardless of this plugin. False whenever WooCommerce is not active. This describes the site, not the caller: a role exemption does not change it.'=>'True when customers cannot leave a WooCommerce product review. Reviews are usually just comments on the "product" post type, so this is mostly the answer for reviews specifically, which "disabled_post_types" does not give you in a form a store owner would recognise. It can also be true on its own: "review" appearing in "blocked_comment_types" closes reviews while comments on products stay open, and WooCommerce\'s own review setting being off closes them regardless of this plugin. False whenever WooCommerce is not active. This describes the site, not the caller: a role exemption does not change it.','How many taxonomy or template rules are configured. Zero while "conditional_rules_enabled" is false.'=>'How many taxonomy or template rules are configured. Zero while "conditional_rules_enabled" is false.','True when per-post conditional rules are active. The post-type fields then describe only the starting point: individual posts may differ based on their taxonomy terms, page template or age. Do not infer a single post\'s comment status from "disabled_post_types" alone while this is true.'=>'True when per-post conditional rules are active. The post-type fields then describe only the starting point: individual posts may differ based on their taxonomy terms, page template or age. Do not infer a single post\'s comment status from "disabled_post_types" alone while this is true.','The mirror image of "allowed_comment_types": comment types that are closed even where comments are open, such as "review" for a WooCommerce store that closes product reviews while other comments on products stay open. Creating one of these is rejected with a 403 on both the comment form and the REST API, so check this before submitting — the post-type fields and "comments_disabled_everywhere" will not tell you. Existing comments of these types are untouched and still readable. A type appearing here is never also listed in "allowed_comment_types".'=>'The mirror image of "allowed_comment_types": comment types that are closed even where comments are open, such as "review" for a WooCommerce store that closes product reviews while other comments on products stay open. Creating one of these is rejected with a 403 on both the comment form and the REST API, so check this before submitting — the post-type fields and "comments_disabled_everywhere" will not tell you. Existing comments of these types are untouched and still readable. A type appearing here is never also listed in "allowed_comment_types".','Counted whatever their status: approved, pending, spam and trash. The preview below counts only the ones the mode you picked would delete.'=>'Counted whatever their status: approved, pending, spam, and bin. The preview below counts only the ones the mode you picked would delete.','True when no post type on this site is left accepting comments, including non-public ones the settings screen does not list. Stricter than a "status" of "all", which only means every post type the settings screen offers is switched off — a non-public post type that supports comments can still be open in that case. Comment types listed in "allowed_comment_types" are permitted regardless, so this is not absolute when that list is non-empty. False whenever a conditional "enable" rule exists, since such a rule reopens the posts it matches.'=>'True when no post type on this site is left accepting comments, including non-public ones the settings screen does not list. Stricter than a "status" of "all", which only means every post type the settings screen offers is switched off — a non-public post type that supports comments can still be open in that case. Comment types listed in "allowed_comment_types" are permitted regardless, so this is not absolute when that list is non-empty. False whenever a conditional "enable" rule exists, since such a rule reopens the posts it matches.','Unknown mode. Use "everywhere", "post_types", "comment_types" or "spam".'=>'Unknown mode. Use "everywhere", "post_types", "comment_types" or "spam".','Unknown mode. Use "everywhere", "post_types" or "off".'=>'Unknown mode. Use "everywhere", "post_types" or "off".','How many comments the request matches. On a dry run this is what would be deleted.'=>'How many comments the request matches. On a dry run this is what would be deleted.','How many comments were deleted. Zero on a dry run.'=>'How many comments were deleted. Zero on a dry run.','True when nothing was deleted and this is a count only.'=>'True when nothing was deleted and this is a count only.','Must be true for a real deletion. Ignored when dry_run is true.'=>'Must be true for a real deletion. Ignored when dry_run is true.','When true, report how many comments match and delete nothing. Call this way first, every time.'=>'When true, report how many comments match and delete nothing. Call this way first, every time.','Comment type slugs, when mode is "comment_types". Types on the site\'s allowlist cannot be deleted this way.'=>'Comment type slugs, when mode is "comment_types". Types on the site\'s allowlist cannot be deleted this way.','Post type slugs, when mode is "post_types".'=>'Post type slugs, when mode is "post_types".','What to delete: every comment, everything on given post types, everything of given comment types, or only spam.'=>'What to delete: every comment, everything on given post types, everything of given comment types, or only spam.','Slugs that were requested but are not registered on this site, so they were ignored. An empty list means everything requested was applied.'=>'Slugs that were requested but are not registered on this site, so they were ignored. An empty list means everything requested was applied.','Post type slugs with comments disabled after this call.'=>'Post type slugs with comments disabled after this call.','The status string after this call.'=>'The status string after this call.','The post types that had comments disabled before the call. Together with "previous_mode" this is everything needed to undo it.'=>'The post types that had comments disabled before the call. Together with "previous_mode" this is everything needed to undo it.','The mode this site was in before the call. Send it back with "previous_disabled_post_types" as "post_types" to restore exactly what was there.'=>'The mode this site was in before the call. Send it back with "previous_disabled_post_types" as "post_types" to restore exactly what was there.','The status string before this call, in the same vocabulary as disable-comments/get-status. This is a human-readable summary and is NOT a valid "mode" - to undo, use "previous_mode" and "previous_disabled_post_types" instead.'=>'The status string before this call, in the same vocabulary as disable-comments/get-status. This is a human-readable summary and is NOT a valid "mode" - to undo, use "previous_mode" and "previous_disabled_post_types" instead.','True when the stored configuration actually changed. False means the site was already in the requested state.'=>'True when the stored configuration actually changed. False means the site was already in the requested state.','Must be true. Guards against an unintended call changing the site configuration.'=>'Must be true. Guards against an unintended call changing the site configuration.','Post type slugs to disable comments on. Only used when mode is "post_types". Slugs this site does not register are reported back in unknown_post_types and ignored.'=>'Post type slugs to disable comments on. Only used when mode is "post_types". Slugs this site does not register are reported back in unknown_post_types and ignored.','"everywhere" disables comments on every post type. "post_types" disables them only on the slugs given in post_types. "off" re-enables comments everywhere.'=>'"everywhere" disables comments on every post type. "post_types" disables them only on the slugs given in post_types. "off" re-enables comments everywhere.','This changes the site and was not confirmed. Re-send the same call with confirm set to true.'=>'This changes the site and was not confirmed. Re-send the same call with confirm set to true.','This site is part of a network where each site is configured from the network admin screen. Changing comment settings through this ability is not supported here - use the network admin screen or WP-CLI instead.'=>'This site is part of a network where each site is configured from the network admin screen. Changing comment settings through this ability is not supported here - use the network admin screen or WP-CLI instead.','Delete comments'=>'Delete comments','Changes where comments are disabled on this site. Either turns comments off everywhere, or replaces the list of post types that have comments disabled. This writes the site configuration and takes effect immediately for every visitor. Call disable-comments/get-status first to see the current state, and pass confirm=true to proceed.'=>'Changes where comments are disabled on this site. Either turns comments off everywhere, or replaces the list of post types that have comments disabled. This writes the site configuration and takes effect immediately for every visitor. Call disable-comments/get-status first to see the current state, and pass confirm=true to proceed.','Set comment status'=>'Set comment status','Blocked: %s'=>'Blocked: %s','Counting Blocked Attempts Since'=>'Counting Blocked Attempts Since','No age limit'=>'No age limit','%s day'=>'%s day' . "\0" . '%s days','Auto-close Comments After'=>'Auto-close Comments After','Conditional Rules Configured'=>'Conditional Rules Configured','Conditional Rules'=>'Conditional Rules','%s. Conditional rules then close or reopen comments on individual posts'=>'%s. Conditional rules then close or reopen comments on individual posts','Anonymous'=>'Anonymous','Spam comments'=>'Spam comments','All comments'=>'All comments','That file contains no settings this version recognises.'=>'That file contains no settings this version recognises.','That file was written by a newer version of Disable Comments (format %1$d; this site understands %2$d). Update t